, as some of them might have some nasty secret objectives. This creates an interesting dynamic and add a bit of extra layer on the horror experience.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Noise management</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/2dd788d06b3f25d908c6a272adfe05f4.poster.avif?t=1771506660\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/2dd788d06b3f25d908c6a272adfe05f4.webm?t=1771506660\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/2dd788d06b3f25d908c6a272adfe05f4.mp4?t=1771506660\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Since the alien species on the ship is blind, you will need to be very careful about the sound that you make. But you can also use it to your advantage -  throw items to distract enemies and sneak past them…</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >… or just use flamethrower to scare them away.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fresh items idea</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/cf8b13774bd066bacc3a78aa7bbe5f56.poster.avif?t=1771506660\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/cf8b13774bd066bacc3a78aa7bbe5f56.webm?t=1771506660\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/extras/cf8b13774bd066bacc3a78aa7bbe5f56.mp4?t=1771506660\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Since Nemesis is not a shooter, don’t expect too many weapons. Instead, you will have a different “arsenal” – noise detector, hacking tool or good-old pipe will come in handy in various situations.</p>", "short_description": "NEMESIS DISTRESS is a unique multiplayer Sci-Fi horror experience that aims at creating unforgettable, cinematic moments. Remember – this is NOT a shooter, in Nemesis you are not the hunter. You are the PREY.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/header.jpg?t=1771506660", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/2d35c633dd1d8f89c29a13498625f23167d037bc/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1771506660", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1343620/2d35c633dd1d8f89c29a13498625f23167d037bc/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1771506660", "website": "https://nemesisdistress.com/", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> 64-bit Windows 7 / 64-Bit Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5 @ 3.3 GHz or better, or AMD Ryzen 3 @ 3.1 GHz or better<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 16 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050Ti (4GB), GTX 1060 (3GB), GTX 1650 (4GB) or AMD Radeon R9 280(3GB), AMD Radeon R9 290 (4GB), RX 470 (4GB)<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 12 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system</li></ul>", "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS *:</strong> 64-bit Windows 7 / 64-Bit Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> AMD / Intel CPU running at 3.6 GHz or h